on optimizing function calling in tool-rich language models by implementing routing before reasoning. Addresses efficiency challenges in agentic AI systems. Open-source implementation available with 12 pages, 2 figures, 6 tables.\",\n    \"author\": \"Saurav Singla, Aarav Singla, Advik Gupta, Parnika Gupta\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23078\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"tool use\", \"function calling\", \"efficiency\", \"AI agents\", \"routing\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AutoSaddler: Automatic Harness Optimization with Agent Execution Traces\",\n    \"description\": \"Research on automatic harness optimization using durable updates from agent execution traces. Addresses software testing and agent reliability challenges. 44 pages, 15 figures with project website and code available.\",\n    \"author\": \"Sungho Park, Wonjoong Kim, Rongyuan Tan, Jue Zhang, Wook-Shin Han, Pengfei Gao, Chanyoung Park, Yongqiang Yao, Rao Fu, Elsie Nallipogu, Qingwei Lin, Saravan Rajmohan, Dongmei Zhang\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23041\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"agent execution\", \"software testing\", \"harness optimization\", \"AI agents\", \"traces\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"What Process Evaluation of Coding Agents Actually Measures\",\n    \"description\": \"Research examining evaluation metrics for coding agents, arguing that 'Action, Task, and Step Are Three Different Levels.' Addresses fundamental questions about how we measure and evaluate AI coding agent performance. 38 pages, 8 figures.\",\n    \"author\": \"Jiawei He, Mengyu Shi, Jie Jia, Xikai Yang, Dong Sun\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.22960\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"coding agents\", \"evaluation metrics\", \"benchmarking\", \"AI measurement\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Concepts for Securing Agentic AI Coding and the Terok Environment\",\n    \"description\": \"Research on security concepts for agentic AI coding systems, introducing the Terok environment. To be published at AGENSYS workshop at ECML PKDD 2026. Addresses critical security challenges in AI-powered development environments.\",\n    \"author\": \"Jiří Vyskočil, Franz Pöschel, Andreas Knüpfer\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.22930\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI security\", \"agentic coding\", \"secure development\", \"Terok environment\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Agent-G²: Gaussian Guidance for Agentic Reinforcement Learning\",\n    \"description\": \"Research on Gaussian Guidance for agentic reinforcement learning systems. Code and project page available. Represents advances in training agentic AI systems using novel reinforcement learning approaches.\",\n    \"author\": \"Zixuan Wang, Yanrui Miao, Zhengxi Lu, Teng Pan, Yiwen Qiu, Hongxing Li, Peng Qiu, Ruiqing Zhang, Yongliang Shen\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23318\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"agentic AI\", \"reinforcement learning\", \"Gaussian guidance\", \"AI agents\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"SRPO: Self-Reflective Policy Optimization for Long-Horizon Reasoning\",\n    \"description\": \"Research on Self-Reflective Policy Optimization (SRPO) for long-horizon reasoning tasks. Accepted to ICML 2026. Addresses challenges in maintaining coherent reasoning across extended tasks.\",\n    \"author\": \"Jialong Liu, Yuling Shi, Ning Yang, Xiaodong Gu, Zuchao Li\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23493\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"long-horizon reasoning\", \"policy optimization\", \"ICML 2026\", \"self-reflection\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"From Generation to Simulation: How Far Are World Models from Being True Simulators?\",\n    \"description\": \"42-page paper examining how far world models are from being true simulators. With 23 figures and 2 tables. Project page available. Addresses fundamental questions about world model capabilities and limitations.\",\n    \"author\": \"Tong Wang, Huan Deng, Mucheng Yang, Yang He, Xiaohui Kuang, Gang Zhao\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23070\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"world models\", \"simulation\", \"AI agents\", \"model evaluation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"LLM-based Agents for Forecasting and Prediction: Methods, Training, Evaluation, and Applications\",\n    \"description\": \"Comprehensive survey on LLM-based agents for forecasting and prediction tasks. Covers methods, training, evaluation, and applications. Represents state-of-the-art understanding of predictive AI systems.\",\n    \"author\": \"Xiaogang Xu, Jiaqi Tang, Jianmin Chen, Yingying Yan, Zhenchao Tang, Xiangxin Zhou, Xiaobin Hu, Wei Wei, Jinfeng Wu, Qifeng Chen, Lu Zhou, Jiafei Wu, Zhe Liu, Jianwei Yin, Weimin Zheng\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23058\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"LLM agents\", \"forecasting\", \"prediction\", \"survey\", \"evaluation\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"PsychJail: Exploring Psychological Jailbreaks via Multi-Turn Persuasion of LLM Policies\",\n    \"description\": \"Research on psychological jailbreaking techniques using multi-turn persuasion strategies to manipulate LLM policies. Addresses AI safety and security challenges.\",\n    \"author\": \"Zeyu Feng, Qingyu Wu, Yuzhe Luo, Hua Cheng\",\n    \"source\": \"ArXiv\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23028\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"topics\": [\"jailbreaking\", \"LLM security\", \"psychological manipulation\", \"AI safety\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  }\n]\n",
      "numLines": 143,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 143
    }
  }
